a system-level intelligent
and optimization.

00:39:01.806 --> 00:39:05.845
Also, we could have the platform

00:39:05.846 --> 00:39:08.080
to support Deep Learning

00:39:08.081 --> 00:39:10.555
and the intelligence exploration.

00:39:10.556 --> 00:39:14.155
Based upon the platform,
you can build,

00:39:14.156 --> 00:39:18.060
share the results for
practice or for education,

00:39:18.061 --> 00:39:21.130
and also the platform can
petition a host that the label,

00:39:21.131 --> 00:39:22.895
the Deep Learning data.

00:39:22.896 --> 00:39:24.930
Also, you can leverage

00:39:24.931 --> 00:39:28.150
the platform and also
leverage the tools

00:39:28.151 --> 00:39:31.540
for management integration and

00:39:31.541 --> 00:39:33.405
the AI lifecycle management,

00:39:33.406 --> 00:39:36.535
or also compiler optimization.

00:39:36.536 --> 00:39:43.830
The cognitive capability
built on the platform,

00:39:43.831 --> 00:39:45.580
including natural language,

00:39:45.581 --> 00:39:47.590
understanding visual perception,

00:39:47.591 --> 00:39:49.510
speech and recognition, as I

00:39:49.511 --> 00:39:52.810
mentioned, across
different domain.

00:39:53.040 --> 00:39:58.005
So let me focus on
the middle layer,

00:39:58.006 --> 00:40:02.725
the platform to manage
the heterogeneous cluster.

00:40:02.726 --> 00:40:08.165
So we open sourced a
PAI called the OpenPAI,

00:40:08.166 --> 00:40:09.870
a platform for AI.

00:40:09.871 --> 00:40:11.795
So this platform is

00:40:11.796 --> 00:40:16.355
GPU cluster management
infrastructure.

00:40:16.356 --> 00:40:21.910
It has the following features:
First, it's open.

00:40:21.911 --> 00:40:23.640
So it's open source,

00:40:23.641 --> 00:40:27.675
it's licensed under MIT license,

00:40:27.676 --> 00:40:29.570
and it's actually operated in

00:40:29.571 --> 00:40:31.515
the open collaboration model.

00:40:31.516 --> 00:40:34.950
We actually work with
various partners,

00:40:34.951 --> 00:40:37.140
I will mention the details later,

00:40:37.141 --> 00:40:42.620
and to develop and evolve
the platform together.

00:40:42.621 --> 00:40:46.645
The OpenPAI is
actually extensible.

00:40:46.646 --> 00:40:49.230
It not only support

00:40:49.231 --> 00:40:52.065
all the major Deep
Learning frameworks,

00:40:52.066 --> 00:40:54.280
it also, I mean,

00:40:54.281 --> 00:40:57.670
extensible to support
a new workload.

00:40:57.671 --> 00:40:59.420
It also supported,

00:40:59.421 --> 00:41:02.830
diversify their hardware
including FPGA,

00:41:02.831 --> 00:41:04.425
GPU, and the ASIC,

00:41:04.426 --> 00:41:08.525
given that the drivers
are available.

00:41:08.526 --> 00:41:13.650
OpenPAI has a modular design.

00:41:13.651 --> 00:41:16.020
So, you actually embraced

00:41:16.021 --> 00:41:20.590
the microservice design paradigm.

00:41:20.591 --> 00:41:24.210
So, every service
run in a container.

00:41:24.211 --> 00:41:27.610
So this microservice choice

00:41:27.611 --> 00:41:33.310
can help us replace
a certain component,

00:41:33.311 --> 00:41:34.610
PAI component are very easily,

00:41:34.611 --> 00:41:36.205
for example, if you would like to

00:41:36.206 --> 00:41:38.805
try a different storage option,

00:41:38.806 --> 00:41:41.050
you can switch from,

00:41:41.051 --> 00:41:44.910
for example, HDFS to cluster FS.

00:41:44.911 --> 00:41:50.185
PAI also have a good efficiency.

00:41:50.186 --> 00:41:53.640
It supports fine-grained
the GPO scheduling,

00:41:53.641 --> 00:41:55.360
it also support
high-speed network

00:41:55.361 --> 00:41:58.545
including RDMA extension.

00:41:58.546 --> 00:42:02.870
PAI also has a relatively
good manageability.

00:42:02.871 --> 00:42:06.970
It actually provide a web UI for

00:42:06.971 --> 00:42:13.005
platform operator to manage
and monitor the platform.

00:42:13.006 --> 00:42:18.870
It also help the Deep
Learning user to manage job,

00:42:18.871 --> 00:42:20.430
a submission job, or

00:42:20.431 --> 00:42:25.245
even monitor the
hardware utilization.

00:42:25.246 --> 00:42:28.875
PAI provides some
fault-tolerance capability.

00:42:28.876 --> 00:42:34.840
So you don't have to
worry about the failure.

00:42:36.210 --> 00:42:39.120
Also, PAI learns a lot

00:42:39.121 --> 00:42:42.555
from Microsoft's
internal practice.

00:42:42.556 --> 00:42:50.390
So, we actually reproduce
the production environment and

00:42:50.391 --> 00:42:56.730
the realistic
industrial usage case

00:42:56.731 --> 00:43:01.860
for a Deep Learning
model training scenario.

00:43:02.090 --> 00:43:05.610
Here is a high level overview

00:43:05.611 --> 00:43:08.785
of the OpenPAI architecture.

00:43:08.786 --> 00:43:10.860
The underlying is

00:43:10.861 --> 00:43:14.990
the host environment
that including Cloud.

00:43:14.991 --> 00:43:20.755
Private Cloud, or
on-premise cluster.

00:43:20.756 --> 00:43:24.685
That's running on top of
heterogeneous hardware,

00:43:24.686 --> 00:43:28.270
GPU, CPU, FPGA, RDMA, etc.

00:43:28.271 --> 00:43:31.560
On top of that, we support,

00:43:31.561 --> 00:43:34.055
we leverage Docker and Kubernetes

00:43:34.056 --> 00:43:37.715
to perform container
orchestration,

00:43:37.716 --> 00:43:40.640
and we provide tools to deploy

00:43:40.641 --> 00:43:42.940
the platform easily and

00:43:42.941 --> 00:43:46.470
also to upgrade
and maintain this.

00:43:46.471 --> 00:43:51.375
Also, we have job management,
resource management, etc.

00:43:51.376 --> 00:43:57.305
So, one of the key things
in market as read, is that,

00:43:57.306 --> 00:44:00.920
we try to provide a
standardized interface

00:44:00.921 --> 00:44:05.120
to the deep learning workload,

00:44:05.121 --> 00:44:09.780
and to the platform
management tools.

00:44:09.781 --> 00:44:14.260
So, that as long as
the interface are centralized,

00:44:15.320 --> 00:44:18.225
all the deep learning workloads

00:44:18.226 --> 00:44:21.750
or traditional big data workload

00:44:21.751 --> 00:44:24.650
can leverage this
centralized API to run

00:44:24.651 --> 00:44:28.365
on this open pipe platform.

00:44:28.366 --> 00:44:33.185
This would ensure
the portability of the workload.

00:44:33.186 --> 00:44:37.840
Meaning that once you

00:44:37.841 --> 00:44:40.720
successfully run
deep learning job in

00:44:40.721 --> 00:44:43.980
one PAI cluster instance,

00:44:43.981 --> 00:44:51.415
it can apply to running on
other PAI deployment as well.

00:44:51.416 --> 00:44:56.790
Also, this interface and
the runtime support enabled

00:44:56.791 --> 00:45:03.790
the innovation of high level
AI service like AutoML, etc.

00:45:04.560 --> 00:45:07.250
Here is a little bit more details

00:45:07.251 --> 00:45:09.970
of the our current
implementation.

00:45:09.971 --> 00:45:13.625
For example, as I
mentioned I use Docker,

00:45:13.626 --> 00:45:16.895
we use Kubernetes for
cluster management.

00:45:16.896 --> 00:45:19.540
On top of that, for storage,

00:45:19.541 --> 00:45:23.570
our current storage option
is HDFS because that is one

00:45:23.571 --> 00:45:27.775
of the most popular
distributed storage solution.

00:45:27.776 --> 00:45:33.295
We use Hadoop with
our own extension of GPU support

00:45:33.296 --> 00:45:37.240
for complicated GPU scheduling

00:45:37.241 --> 00:45:40.390
